# Settings tabs

Joelboard Ajustes are **tabbed**. Do not flatten Hub or app settings into a single scrolling list.

- Markup: `.set-tabs` / `.set-tab` / `.set-pane` (core styles in `public/joelboard.css`; `JB.switchSet(name, root)`).
- Default first tab is **Tema**. Extra app stuff gets its own tab (Perfil, Calendar, Sobre, …).
- Hub uses `#hubSet` and `switchHubSet`. Apps use `#setOverlay`.
- New apps: copy Notes — tabs in the overlay, panes hidden until selected.

## Equal pane height

Every settings tab must keep the **same modal height** when switching panes. Do not let short tabs shrink the sheet or tall tabs resize it.

- `#setOverlay .modal` and `#hubSet .modal` use a fixed height (`min(640px, 88vh)` / `92vh` on mobile) with flex column layout.
- `.set-pane` fills the remaining space and scrolls inside (`overflow-y: auto`). Header, tabs, and footer actions stay outside the scroll.
- Do not remove that height lock or go back to content-sized modals for Ajustes.
- Prefer `display: none` / `.active` on panes (existing pattern); the visible pane still fills the locked height.
